  "outcome": "Baseline legacy-type selection fails; adapted actual backend syntax passes Linux host, gfx1013 device and Prospero host.",
  "recommendation": [
    "Use an explicit hash-guarded client adaptation selecting modern compute/data types by actual hipBLAS major version. Keep official headers and HIP version unchanged; no persistent fork is necessary.",
    "Modern GemmEx APIs distinguish hipDataType for buffers from hipblasComputeType_t for arithmetic; never cast old datatype enum numerics into compute enum.",
    "Keep current snapshot header set authenticated as future selected dependency only after review; this experiment changes no dependency lock.",
    "Implement and numerically test seven imported entry points with honest unsupported handling: context create/destroy, stream association, SGEMM, GemmEx, pointer-batched and strided-batched GemmEx. Do not equate successful header compilation with BLAS availability."
